abstract: "This dataset collection contains phytoplankton and zooplankton observations\
  \ from coastal British Columbia, Canada, and Southeast Alaska, United States.\n\n\
  \nPhytoplankton observations include:\n- Sentinel 3A and 3B chlorophyll-a (Chla)\
  \ and suspended particulate matter (SPM) imagery for coastal and offshore British\
  \ Columbia (BC) and Southeast Alaska waters, both as daily and 8 day averages\n\
  - Concentrations of phytoplankton pigments from High-Performance Liquid Chromatography\
  \ (HPLC) analysis of water collected from niskin bottles, to estimate phytoplankton\
  \ group-level biomass contributions within bulk water samples in the Northern Salish\
  \ Sea and Central Coast from 2015-2025\n- Chlorophyll and phaeopigment concentrations\
  \ from water collected from niskin bottles, collected from 2017 to 2026 within the\
  \ Calvert Island, Johnstone Strait, and the Quadra Island study regions \n- Protistan\
  \ plankton community composition, via optical microscopy, at multiple time series\
  \ and spatial survey stations across the northern Salish Sea (Strait of Georgia)\
  \ and central coast, and within False Creek, British Columbia from 2016 - 2025\n\
  \n\nZooplankton observations include:\n- Size-fractionated zooplankton biomass and\
  \ isotope data obtained from collecting samples with vertical net hauls from 2014\
  \ to 2026 within the Calvert Island, Johnstone Strait, and the Quadra Island study\
  \ regions \n- Zooplankton abundance and biomass data obtained from analyzing microscopy\
  \ samples collected with vertical net hauls from 2016 to 2024 within the Calvert\
  \ Island, Johnstone Strait, and the Quadra Island study regions \n- Fatty acids\
  \ of particulate matter collected from 2015 to 2018 near Quadra Island, British\
  \ Columbia, Canada \n- Mesozooplankton taxonomy data collected from the northern\
  \ Strait of Georgia, Discovery Islands, Johnstone Strait, and Queen Charlotte Strait\
  \ from April to July of 2015 and 2016"
